WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.900
<b>Nanba Building 5</b>

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:11.650
There, all done.

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:14.410
Yay! Thanks, old man!

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:17.780
Um... Could you not call me that?

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.810
Thanks, Old Man Qi!

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.470
Uh, yeah... This old man is glad.

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:24.500
Something wrong?

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:29.640
No, I was just thinking about the 
attack charm on Rokuriki-san.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.520
I don't think that belonged to Enki.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.300
When I burned the charm earlier,

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.430
I felt the chi flow, but it was strange.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:43.810
Are you saying someone other than 
Enki is able to use the attack charm?

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.850
If so, who?

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:52.260
Hey, please wake up.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.200
I want to ask you something.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.980
Rokuriki-san, please wake up.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:00.030
Hey, stop that! He's injured.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:23.430
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:33.000
<b>Washed Away...</b>

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.180
Upsy-daisy.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:36.580
Speaking of which,

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:40.530
I wonder what happened to the two guys 
who are always with Rokuriki-san.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.620
You mean Youriki-san and Kokoriki-san?

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.450
I didn't see them.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.480
We should keep on moving for now.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.340
But we blocked the pathway 
to the underground.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.970
Don't worry.

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:58.200
There's a hidden passageway here.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.620
I found it by chance,
and that's how I got here.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.050
Hey, Master...

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.120
What is it?

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:09.060
There are very dangerous escaped 
convicts in Building 5 right now,

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:11.870
just like that Mr. Pig, right?

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:17.580
And, um... I heard this Enki-san 
person killed an inmate.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.870
I know you're all strong, but I...

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:24.890
I'm starting to feel really scared.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.970
If something happens to you, I...

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:31.160
We're not going to do battle.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.310
We're going to protect this building.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:34.400
Huh?

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:38.250
We just want to take back the
Building 5 that he supervised.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:41.650
After we betrayed Hachiman,

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:43.360
the organization fell apart,

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:48.340
and we were all sent to a prison in Sichuan.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.080
What's this?

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.290
That's where I met him.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.670
It's a gift for you.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:00.170
A gift? From who?

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.680
From your family.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.110
Why?

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:11.220
They're supposed to think I'm dead!

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:14.940
What's wrong with telling them 
that a living person is alive?

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:18.070
I just wanted to clarify things.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.720
Don't make any more trouble.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:28.740
It was something as simple as that,

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:32.200
but I respect that part of him.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.850
If someone does something for you,

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.580
you want to do something in return.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.090
You're the same way, right?

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:42.170
You're...

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.590
I thought you must be 
uncomfortable in those restraints.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:52.770
Yeah!

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:55.580
<i>If someone does something for you,</i>

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:57.200
<i>you want to do something in return.</i>

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:01.640
<i>Just by thinking that, 
nothing is scary anymore.</i>

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:08.800
<i>I know what I told Jyugo,</i>

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:11.200
<i>but I wonder if that was a good idea.</i>

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:18.390
<i>When did Yamato-dono and Rock start 
acting strange in the first place?</i>

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:20.990
Tsukumo!

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:24.040
Why don't you come and take a break, too?

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:26.180
Join us for a snack.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:30.300
No, there are still some things 
I want to learn from Liang-dono.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:33.360
Yeah? Okay, see ya later, then.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.930
We'll be right back, so wait for us.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:42.340
<i>They were still normal at that time.</i>

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:45.240
<i>Then does that mean...</i>

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:52.410
<i>No, I'm overthinking this.</i>

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:53.450
What?

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:56.950
Why do I have to stay at 
her bedside again today?!

00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:58.480
It can't be helped!

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:00.220
You brought her here,

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:02.170
so you take care of her.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:06.670
She's been unconscious since 
she was brought here yesterday.

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.680
She finally woke up this morning.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.450
I normally don't take in civilians,

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:14.410
but it was an emergency.

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:18.460
It's only natural for a deputy supervisor 
like yourself to stay with her.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:20.690
Besides, you know her.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.760
Oh, man...

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:25.310
The ship for visitors has already sailed.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:27.660
I guess she'll have to stay here today, too.

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:31.570
I have my deputy supervisor
duties too, though.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.080
But...

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:39.180
Big Sister Noriko has always been weak.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:43.090
It's not like she'd be able to see 
Enki-san by coming all the way here.

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.560
Or could it be...

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.440
that she doesn't know?

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.590
Stop, Uno!

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:55.220
Lemme go! I'm going back!

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:57.670
You idiot! What's the point in going back?!

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.780
I'm gonna bring back Nico!

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:00.960
Don't be stupid!

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:02.860
It was dangerous just to get here!

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:03.840
He's right.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.110
There's no guarantee we'll 
be able to come back.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:08.580
No, I'm going back!

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:09.740
Let's go, Jyugo!

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.120
Idiot! Even if he is up there,

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:14.560
that Chinese guy is with him, right?!

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:17.470
You two will just get in the way!

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:21.380
If he's hiding up there, he'll actually be safer.

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:23.750
Let's bet on that possibility.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.420
But... then...

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:29.000
Don't just stand there!
You say something, too.

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:30.500
Uh...

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:32.510
Yeah...

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.000
What's that sound?

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:36.890
Huh?

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:44.650
No way!

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:54.420
This sucks.

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:57.380
That must've been a trap, too.

00:07:57.380 --> 00:07:59.290
So damn annoying.

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:03.040
I wasn't ready for that.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.570
Hey, Jyugo, you okay?

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:06.920
Jyugo?

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:10.170
Hey! Jyugo!

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:13.040
Seriously? He drowned in such a short time?

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:14.290
Is he a genius?

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:16.940
You opened the underground
passageway's lock while drowning?

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:18.290
You're a genius!

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:20.680
Shut up and help him already,
you two imbeciles!

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:23.430
By "help," you mean... that?

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:25.250
Yeah, that!

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:27.310
Someone has to do it, or Jyugo will die!

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.020
I guess so.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:31.320
We should do rock-paper-scissors, then.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.420
Ready... Rock, paper, scissors!

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:38.500
Hey, maybe we should forget about him.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:39.900
I think it's too late anyway.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:41.830
Just get on with it!

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.510
Oh, damn it!

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:44.830
I'll get you for this!

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:55.340
<b>Please Stand By</b>

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:58.210
I... I thought I was gonna die.

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:00.600
That's my line, you idiot.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:02.600
<b>Gogyousan
Underground Level 2</b>

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:06.670
At any rate, we know we're definitely 
in the underground's second level.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:08.610
Let's keep moving.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:13.800
The structure is just as Liang said,

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:16.120
but it's unusually quiet...

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.740
I don't sense any of those 
strange-looking dolls, either.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:24.040
What are you doing, Trois?

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:26.030
There's nothing there.

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:29.130
Yeah, I'm just curious about something.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:32.830
This is it.

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.630
This may be my only chance to see it.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:39.690
Jyugo-kun, can you please open this door?

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:45.900
What's this place?

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.460
I can't see anything.

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:50.150
Wait a moment, I'll turn on the lights.

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:58.780
Idiot! Don't scream! They'll find us!

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:02.590
Damn it, Trois!

00:10:02.590 --> 00:10:04.540
What the hell is this place?!

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:09.200
It's probably a room where they manage 
and maintain those jiangshi-like dolls.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:12.790
Why come all this way to 
see something so creepy?!

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:15.570
I thought if we understood
their internal structure,

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:18.060
we could come up with a
countermeasure to use against them.

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:23.310
I see.

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:26.220
You can insert various weapons internally...

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:30.510
The body is created the same way as a human's.

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:34.120
It's covered with materials 
similar to skin and veins,

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:36.080
though some parts are peeling off.

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.570
Bleurgh...

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:41.940
Ah...

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:45.330
A specialized tool is required 
to further dismantle it.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:47.760
This is very well-designed.

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:50.840
Hey, it's pointless to dismantle that thing.

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:53.400
Let's just go find Kiji-san.

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:56.440
Sorry, give me just a little bit more...

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.460
This is pretty interesting.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:08.730
Jeez...

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:11.700
This is what happens whenever 
he sees a woman or a machine.

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:14.520
Such a broad range of hobbies...

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:16.980
Let's check out the outside 
for the time being.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.320
Why are you just standing there?

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:24.170
You're the only one who can open the lock.

00:11:24.170 --> 00:11:25.790
R-Right...

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:32.700
It's surprisingly quiet.

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:34.550
Even those freaky dolls aren't around.

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:39.640
Maybe they're concentrated around 
the people who got caught, like us.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:42.030
Does that mean no one's here?

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:44.510
If so, it would make our job a lot easier.

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:51.770
So, have you known that guy for long?

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:54.040
Huh? You mean Jyugo?

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:57.300
We ended up in the same prison lots of times,

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:59.450
and we sometimes escaped together,

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:01.530
so I guess I've known him for a while.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:05.420
How can you hang out with a guy when you 
have no idea what he's thinking about?

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:07.930
He's so dimwitted, it pisses me off.

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:12.560
I could never tell what was on 
his mind in the first place,

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.650
so I'm used to it.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:18.120
It won't bother you once you know 
he's just that kind of person.

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:20.140
Is that so?

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:23.930
Besides, I think someone 
who you can't read at all

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:27.550
is more interesting than a person 
you can read like a book.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:34.940
You'll eventually start to get 
to know him, somewhat.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.580
I don't know about that.

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:43.990
I come here to investigate
the noise, only to find rats.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:50.990
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:56.000
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:12:56.550 --> 00:13:00.250
I don't know how you guys 
escaped from your cells,

00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:04.570
but you've got some nerve.

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:07.010
You need to be punished.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:08.650
A queer!

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:10.760
We come all the way here and
find a queer?! Have mercy!

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:12.520
Why are you crying?!

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:15.740
To encounter a queer when we're 
on our way to save a queer!

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:17.360
Like that saying, "go for wool 
and come back shorn?!

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:19.300
Not another queer! What a drag!

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:21.020
I said stop crying!

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:24.280
You guys are being loud. What's going—

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:25.780
Yoo-hoo.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:29.780
Sorry, but we already have a queer.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.540
Don't call me a queer!

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:32.660
Now, see here!

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:35.540
Don't lump me in with that
bastard in heavy makeup!

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:36.590
He's a queer!

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:37.680
I'm a queen!

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:41.040
We're completely different! Got that?!

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:46.680
Is that like... spotted garden eels
and splendid garden eels?

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.500
Zaru soba and mori soba?

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:50.300
Or somen and hiyamugi?

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:54.010
Isn't there a Japanese idiom 
used in this situation?

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:55.460
Was it "almonds comparing their heights"?

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:57.940
No, it's "lentils comparing their heights."

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:01.190
No, you idiot! It's "beans
comparing their heights."

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:02.820
It's about acorns.

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:07.590
You guys have a lot of gall.

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:09.320
I hope you're prepared.

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:11.250
The queer's angry!

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.220
I told you to stop crying!

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:15.080
You're gonna get it now!

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:25.410
These guys...

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:28.920
Those things on their heads remind 
me of the guy from the first level.

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:29.840
Yeah...

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:31.450
That black charm, right?

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:32.850
There's no doubt about it.

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:34.850
Which means...

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:38.210
I knew it!

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:39.850
We gotta run away again!

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:41.690
I won't let you escape!

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:44.080
You two! Attack!

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:47.860
Hurry!

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.670
Whoa! These guys are fast!

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:52.870
Stay away!

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:56.460
You guys are more trouble than you're worth.

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:59.240
Don't underestimate Building 5's guards.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.880
Hey, Ruka!

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.950
I've had it with you!

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:05.380
Are you listening?!

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.140
Answer me, damn it!

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:11.640
Shut up. You're a captive now.

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:15.160
Do you think you can get away with this?!

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:18.640
To treat my beautiful body 
like this is a serious crime!

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:19.730
Oh, my.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:23.330
You're going to ruin your makeup 
if you keep frowning like that.

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:27.150
Shut it! And give me back my makeup kit!

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:31.650
As if. You're going to stay put for a while.

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:33.700
How long is a while?

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:36.910
Until that heavy makeup flakes off.

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:39.140
When pigs fly!

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:41.410
At least hand me a mirror!

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:48.420
Jyugo! As always, you're so slow!

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.800
If you don't wanna die, run, you idiot!

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:55.040
Anyway, those screams earlier...

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:57.810
They'd better not have been inmates.

00:15:58.010 --> 00:16:01.500
Oh, at least your sense of hearing is sharp.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:03.730
Inmates from your building were here, too.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:05.190
Wh-What did you say?!

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:08.450
Running away is all they can do.

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:12.510
People from other buildings 
are so weak, it's laughable!

00:16:14.350 --> 00:16:17.030
Hey, Ruka... I have one question.

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:18.150
What?

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:19.920
The inmates from my building...

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:22.460
They were handsome, right?

00:16:23.050 --> 00:16:25.460
Yeah, their faces were
their only good feature.

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:30.410
<i>I can't allow my adorable 
inmates to be in danger.</i>

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:34.970
I'll give you something nice
if you'll let me out.

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:36.490
Something nice?

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:40.660
There's a custom-made 
toner in my makeup kit.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:46.100
Believe it or not, it's made with
a 100% hyaluronic acid formula!

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:49.890
O-One hundred percent?

00:16:49.890 --> 00:16:51.570
That's basically a liquid concentrate.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:57.270
The audacity to call that a toner, 
and that insatiable desire for beauty...

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:02.130
Well? My firm skin is enough 
of a testament to it, right?

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:05.420
You'd better start taking care
of your skin, or you'll regret it.

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.850
<i>H-He's right...</i>

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:11.140
<i>I can't deny my concerns about
the crow's feet I'm developing</i>

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:13.010
<i>thanks to my long imprisonment.</i>

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.270
So?

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:17.140
<i>I want that hyaluronic acid!</i>

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:20.880
If you accept now, I'll even throw 
in my sunscreen cream, as well!

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:22.770
It's SPF 60!

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:25.600
S-SPF 60?!

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:29.300
There's been so much innovation
since I've been locked away!

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:32.650
<i>As if that actually exists.</i>

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:38.070
<i>I need UV protection,
since I'll be going outside soon.</i>

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:40.910
I'll give you both.

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:44.600
<i>But there's no way I can betray Enki-san!</i>

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:47.080
<i>Hyaluronic acid! Enki-san!</i>

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.670
<i>What should I do?!</i>

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.460
How far are we now?!

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:55.490
I don't know, but we can't stop!

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:57.930
We need to find a way to
the third underground level!

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:02.480
Searching for something at 
a time like this?! Like hell!

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:04.430
We'll be killed the moment we stop!

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:05.600
I know that!

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:08.100
That's why I'm thinking of a plan!

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:09.890
Well, think of one quick, you idiot!

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:12.610
Then <i>you</i> come up with one, you idiot!

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:15.740
Okay, please step aside for a moment.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:28.290
Not bad for a makeshift weapon.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:30.390
Damn you, Trois! What the hell?!

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:31.780
You nearly killed us!

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:35.020
You guys looked so awesome 
when you blew away.

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:36.990
Like some kind of Super Sentai team.

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:38.260
Shut up!

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.320
What the hell is that, anyway?!

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:41.520
Where did you find it?!

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:45.250
I made it from dismantled parts and scraps.

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:47.770
There was a surprising
amount of useful material!

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:51.020
Oh, you mean parts from
that jiangshi you dismantled.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:54.520
But didn't you say you needed a 
special tool for that, or something?

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:57.280
Oh, you mean this?

00:18:57.670 --> 00:19:00.000
Wh-Why do you have that?

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:03.030
I found it in that room on the first level.

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:05.300
I was curious about the odd shape,

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:07.060
so I brought it with me.

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:11.810
To think it would come in handy here.

00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:15.960
It's all thanks to someone who 
left everything unlocked.

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:20.110
<i>Come to think of it, I think 
I unlocked the drawers, too.</i>

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:22.220
All I had to do was dismantle 
one and put it together.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:27.470
Man, it's been a while since I 
got to do this. It's so much fun.

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:29.260
That tool...

00:19:29.260 --> 00:19:31.940
He must've stolen it from 
Kazari-san's job site.

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:34.530
Stealing? How cunning.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:38.060
Well, it's not my proudest moment,

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:40.240
but drastic circumstances 
call for drastic measures.

00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:43.240
Don't tell Kiji-san, okay?

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.890
Oh, shit! Hey, we better run!
This is not good!

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:48.870
What? What's he planning to do?

00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:53.880
It's a bit flashy, but it's pretty handy.

00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:02.130
Trois is amazing!

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:06.310
I had no idea he was that crazy.

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:09.270
I thought he was just a 
perverted lingerie thief.

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:15.410
Yeah, he escaped his previous prison 
just like this, and then again after that.

00:20:15.410 --> 00:20:17.640
Before he knew it, he was here.

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:21.530
Trois is only trying to surprise them,

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:25.030
but no matter how you 
look at it, that's overkill.

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:30.560
Whatever. This is our chance.

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:32.290
Let's get out of here now.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.290
Agreed.

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:40.120
Jyugo! What are you doing? Let's go!

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:43.640
You're the only one who can unlock the doors!

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:45.300
Y-Yeah...

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:48.300
<i>I see...</i>

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:52.060
<i>So he's the "key."</i>

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:56.560
Crap! Let me go!

00:20:56.980 --> 00:21:00.560
Where do you guys think you're going?

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:04.200
There's no point in going down any further.

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:05.770
What are you planning?

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:11.330
Not that I'm really interested in what 
goes through the minds of inmates.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:13.450
Jyugo!

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:18.460
I just like finding out people's secrets.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:24.720
Though, I don't think you can 
get anywhere without this guy.

00:21:27.280 --> 00:21:30.080
You no longer have your "key,"

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:32.510
so give up and confess.

00:21:34.900 --> 00:21:37.230
<i>Why did he get caught at a time like this?</i>

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:41.730
<i>He's been dragging his feet all this time.</i>

00:21:44.080 --> 00:21:46.240
<i>He really...</i>

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:48.550
<i>pisses me off!</i>

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:28.560
I know where that kappa guy is!

00:23:28.560 --> 00:23:30.430
It's finally our turn.

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:32.470
We'll pay our debts, so don't interfere.

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:35.970
We'll show you our awesome escape technique.

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:38.310
Next episode: "Sound and Words."

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Sound and Words</b>
